# GitHub issue types (OBRA_APP)

**Scope:** Apply this rule only when the conversation or task is about **GitHub issues** (create, update, epics, sub-issues) or **`user-github`** MCP issue operations for this repo—not for general coding.

**Feature** and **Task** are **issue types** (GitHub Issues types), not labels. Set them with the **`type`** argument on **`issue_write`**, not with **`labels`**.

| Type | Use |
|------|-----|
| **Feature** | Parent / epic / high-level tracking issues that group multiple work items (product-facing scope). |
| **Task** | Sub-issues or standalone implementation tickets under a feature (concrete deliverables). |

## Conventions

- Set **`type`** to **Feature** on the epic only; set **`type`** to **Task** on child / implementation issues.
- For **Digital-Craft-AR**, configured issue types include **`Feature`**, **`Task`**, and **`Bug`** (use **`list_issue_types`** via GitHub MCP if GitHub’s API expects a different identifier in edge cases).
- **Labels** are separate: use **`labels`** only for tags unrelated to this Feature/Task split. If you update **`labels`**, merge with existing labels so you do not drop unrelated tags.
